    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d210-a1">

                <pb facs="0305" n="197" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg197"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 12.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lane to Mr. Quincy.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Pacific Mail Steamship Company</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-06-01"><hi rendition="#italic">June 1,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In case the State Department has not received from the U. S. consular agent at
                    Corinto any advices respecting the pointing a loaded Krupp breech-loading gun
                    against this company’s steamer <hi rendition="#italic">San José</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">City of New York</hi>, we beg to hand you copy of a
                    letter from our general agent at San Francisco, dated May 25, together with copy
                    of official report of the U. S. consular agent at Corinto, under date of May 11,
                    to Capt. F. H. Johnston, commanding this company’s steamship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">City of New York</hi>, all of which explain themselves
                    and which we submit to the Department for such action as may be deemed
                    proper.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. H. Lane</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
